{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787548115891441001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"lemuroid-compliant-hoopoe","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"3cf2d6e6d0c2262d457ea0f85b62d276816d55c5fc4ceeca2dd74a43a9444cd5","event_uuid":"42058d0b-d70a-4e2e-ac25-d44179433a24","position":{"commit_sha":"b3c722a8263ae4ce95875d1fce7772c38dd9b100","position":"1787542691850644001-42058d0b-d70a-4e2e-ac25-d44179433a24"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"829fe953f3cb6fb37b569374ea209c7d2861028be30fb4fb190786ee9aa39678","event_uuid":"a16d2c90-eebb-4d73-b3ec-02bfd8588f92","position":{"commit_sha":"65c785382ae6be6515f81d7da103f583bc3a1165","position":"1787542806617586001-a16d2c90-eebb-4d73-b3ec-02bfd8588f92"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"eb19020658c50289216a5defd35a746959f82aa2232388083235e9498f125d0e","event_uuid":"7686cf91-488b-4cff-8c76-7cd876a336f1","position":{"commit_sha":"55f1f6385570ac0018f9a9d0727d73529dfd21d8","position":"1787542935287311001-7686cf91-488b-4cff-8c76-7cd876a336f1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787542691850644001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a16d2c90-eebb-4d73-b3ec-02bfd8588f92","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4000-2df3-398d-44e2"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nA normal post-merge `review-plan` from the project checkout made zero LLM calls and took 512.139s before failing because `git fetch origin` hit the 300s timeout. The checkout is partial/promisor (`blob:none`) and its `origin.fetch` maps every remote head. Attested ref resolution calls `fetch_origin()` without a ref, which executes `git fetch --quiet --no-filter origin`; this can traverse/materialize the enormous tickets history while only a code SHA is needed. The failed attempt left partial packs, including one approximately 153.6 MB.\n\nA normal retry from a temporary clone whose origin fetch refspec was main-only crossed the fetch boundary and completed the same review with signed PASS. This discriminates broad-ref transfer from model latency. It is distinct from `strained-bare-turnstone`, which addressed intermittent transport stalls and durable voting behavior, and from `grassy-cracked-morpho`, which covers completion close history-times-tracker scanning.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce attested resolution from a partial/promisor checkout whose origin fetch refspec includes both code and the large tickets branch.\n- Change snapshot ref materialization to fetch only the requested code ref/object while preserving fail-closed attestation semantics and support for remote refs.\n- Preserve blob materialization when the requested snapshot requires it without broadening the remote refspec.\n- Add a regression test that records the exact fetch argv/refspec and rejects an unscoped no-filter origin fetch.\n- Measure the fetch boundary before and after with a representative main-only target.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Resolving a specific attested code ref does not fetch unrelated origin heads.\n- [ ] Blobless/promisor checkouts can still materialize the requested snapshot when required.\n- [ ] Missing or unreachable requested refs continue to fail closed.\n- [ ] Tests pin scoped fetch arguments and cover a checkout with an unrelated large branch.\n- [ ] Before/after fetch duration and transferred-object evidence are recorded.\n- [ ] No LLM, gate, or tracker behavior is bypassed.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","reason":"Pass the specific ref/object required by attested snapshot materialization into the fetch seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py","reason":"Scope the network fetch to the requested target without fetching unrelated remote heads."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_snapshot_targeted_fetch.py","reason":"Pin scoped fetch argv and fail-closed behavior in partial/promisor repositories."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["performance","plan-review","git","snapshot"],"ticket_id":"39a2-4832-e436-4850","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Attested ref materialization broad-fetches all origin heads","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["42058d0b-d70a-4e2e-ac25-d44179433a24","a16d2c90-eebb-4d73-b3ec-02bfd8588f92","7686cf91-488b-4cff-8c76-7cd876a336f1"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787548115891441001,"uuid":"a8b2447d-f796-4248-920c-2fa380088bef"}